                    {
                        "translation_id": "3346b3ce-99cc-416d-b18f-d45dd3918b94",
                        "source_entry_id": "c6f9940e-90a3-333f-959c-f39d64fcd100",
                        "source_sense_id": "38ce8fa1-7295-3c0a-ac83-59b72e05f61d",
                        "source_sense_description": "het niet logisch zijn",
                        "target_lang_word": "crookedness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "crookedness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ceef99eb-a9cc-3eca-a85c-5c7e8913ba2d",
                                        "entry_id": "75e391f4-3440-3e16-a127-3638e5a1e630",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being crooked"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ba8a073-5d9d-4f42-a2ef-a74ea3419201",
                                                "sense_id": "ceef99eb-a9cc-3eca-a85c-5c7e8913ba2d",
                                                "text": "The river was full of logs—long, slender, barkless pine logs—and we leaned on the rails of the bridge, and watched the men put them together into rafts. These rafts were of a shape and construction to suit the crookedness and extreme narrowness of the Neckar."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f9a6442-57a1-4597-82ee-4aab20406025",
                                                "sense_id": "ceef99eb-a9cc-3eca-a85c-5c7e8913ba2d",
                                                "text": "But are sailors […] without vices? No; but less often than with landsmen do their vices, so called, partake of crookedness of heart, seeming less to proceed from viciousness than exuberance of vitality after long constraint; frank manifestations in accordance with natural law."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea12485e-ea72-4042-a508-4b202e657d7d",
                                                "sense_id": "ceef99eb-a9cc-3eca-a85c-5c7e8913ba2d",
                                                "text": "She had cost me two tenants and no end of sleep, had heated my temper to boiling, yet, somehow I could not hate that baby. The meanest thing about her was the way she could make you feel yourself. One has to make a living and one must sleep. It is one of the crookednesses of life when a little yellow-haired baby can cause you so much trouble and yet won't even let you hate her."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3c41c155-2153-4481-96e0-7c851a435ccc",
                        "source_entry_id": "c6f9940e-90a3-333f-959c-f39d64fcd100",
                        "source_sense_id": "78af8333-1624-3dea-84f4-d4e018f4cfa3",
                        "source_sense_description": "het niet recht zijn",
                        "target_lang_word": "curvature",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "curvature",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e9cada65-ac81-3ae0-b687-6c1b19f0974e",
                                        "entry_id": "5e89bd86-980a-32aa-a5ec-360528b53c04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The shape of something curved."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9afad349-22db-4d3f-939f-d8a37654a7ec",
                                                "sense_id": "e9cada65-ac81-3ae0-b687-6c1b19f0974e",
                                                "text": "Constructional costs are kept to a minimum by the admissibility of heavy grades and sharp curvature."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02761719-bd68-4c77-91b3-b9d8556052dc",
                                                "sense_id": "e9cada65-ac81-3ae0-b687-6c1b19f0974e",
                                                "text": "In the first of the movie's many striking images, we share his majestic view from the top, the curvature of the planet and the glow of the horizon brilliantly reflected in his helmet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ae986b2-e16e-302f-8f1a-bd7b44a5dcea",
                                        "entry_id": "5e89bd86-980a-32aa-a5ec-360528b53c04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The extent to which a subspace is curved within a metric space."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b42cf6e0-19d4-45fa-9cb1-6c6797acd3a2",
                                                "sense_id": "2ae986b2-e16e-302f-8f1a-bd7b44a5dcea",
                                                "text": "A turtle drawing an ellipse would have to turn more per distance traveled to get around its “pointy” sides than to get around its flatter top and bottom. This notion of how “pointy something is,” expressed as the ratio of angle turned to distance traveled, is the intrinsic quantity that mathematicians call curvature."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "662510e7-046c-3dc8-8e6d-6de58cea1cf3",
                                        "entry_id": "5e89bd86-980a-32aa-a5ec-360528b53c04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The extent to which a Riemannian manifold is intrinsically curved."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
